Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:22:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] soc: nxp: rw: enable ENET reference clock before PHY
 reset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The RMII PHY takes its 50 MHz reference clock from the RW6xx ENET
clock output and must be reset while that clock is running. The ENET
clock gate was only opened by the ENET module device, which
initializes after the PHY device, so the PHY driver reset the PHY
without a clock and it stayed unresponsive.

Open the TDDR ENET clock gate in clock_init() together with the
existing ENET setup, as the MCUXpresso SDK does in
BOARD_InitModuleClock().

Signed-off-by: Tobias Frauenschläger <t.frauenschlaeger@me.com>
(cherry picked from commit 727d0abe869a9c125d238abf8e2ed8d81b156665)
[backport to v4.3.0: no TDDR_PDB re-assert in this context]
---
 soc/nxp/rw/soc.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/soc/nxp/rw/soc.c b/soc/nxp/rw/soc.c
index 166c6008310..af086f142b5 100644
--- a/soc/nxp/rw/soc.c
+++ b/soc/nxp/rw/soc.c
@@ -290,6 +290,8 @@ __weak __ramfunc void clock_init(void)
 #endif
 
 #if DT_NODE_HAS_STATUS_OKAY(DT_NODELABEL(enet)) && CONFIG_NET_L2_ETHERNET
+	/* The PHY needs its 50 MHz reference clock running before it is reset. */
+	CLOCK_EnableClock(kCLOCK_TddrMciEnetClk);
 	RESET_PeripheralReset(kENET_IPG_RST_SHIFT_RSTn);
 	RESET_PeripheralReset(kENET_IPG_S_RST_SHIFT_RSTn);
 #endif
